description:
The future of energy is digitised, decarbonised and localised. At Smartest Energy, we need revolutionary thinkers to help our customers make the most of this new landscape, thinking differently to find smart solutions to complex problems. Join us and help power the revolution.


Formed in 2001, we’re an agile business driven by entrepreneurial thinking. As a subsidiary of the Marubeni Corporation, we also have strong investment and infrastructure behind us. As well as our US office, we have three offices in the UK, and another in Australia. Further expansion will follow shortly which means big global career opportunities for you, with plenty of potential to explore new markets.


Overview

You will lead on the design, development and control of SmartestEnergy US’s data. You will develop knowledge of the underlying data and data products involved in the end to end business and operational processes and be responsible for engaging with business representatives and working closely with internal and external IT partners and vendors to assist in the translation of business requirements into application technical solutions and for their delivery across the portfolio of change initiatives and business processes.

In this position, you will be involved in the following:


Participate in analysis, validation and verification to determine what data is required to support business needs, where it is created, read, updated and deleted and the quality criteria associated with it;
Works with staff, vendors and customers to understand the business requirements to design the data architecture, solutions and processes;
Support wider team problem solving and analysis while balancing data, technology, business and operational issues to identify and deliver viable solutions;
Delivery of customised reports and recommendations to support on-going business decisions and customer reporting requirements;
Analysing large energy market data sets from multiple sources to enable business insights and data driven decision making;
Lead on the development of the critical data artefacts including data models (conceptual, logical and physical);
Ensure alignment of data artefacts through close working relationships with the business and operational stakeholders;
Develops specific metrics for quality and consistency reviews of data.


You are likely to have the following skills/experience:


Graduate in a relevant discipline or area;
Ability to rapidly comprehend the functions and capabilities of new technologies;
Can balance the long-term ("big picture") and short-term implications of individual decisions;
Ability to translate business and customer needs into data requirements;
The ability to communicate complex ideas in a clear, concise manner (verbal and written) across functional and technical departments
Work on multiple tasks at any one time, handling conflicting demands, prioritise workload and effectively delegate while maintaining high quality standards;
Sound judgement, attention to detail, accuracy, and follow-through on actions including the flexibility to perform in an ever-changing work environment;
High emotional resilience and good interpersonal and relationship building skills.


Check out all our current open positions: https://www.smartestenergycareers.com

Our Privacy Policy is here: https://smartestenergy.com/privacy

Responsibilities
1. Develop rigorous analysis using statistical models while working collaboratively to identify highly-impact opportunities related to performance optimization and business value;
2. Research and apply appropriate methods for new analysis;
3. Conduct analysis and build models for performance optimization, media optimization, experimentation, and lift studies, etc.;
4. Conduct data analysis and insightful visualizations.
Qualifications
1. Bachelor or above degree major in Statistics or related fields with 3+ years of hands-on experience in developing statistical models and implementing data science solutions;
2. Familiar with Python or SQL;
3. Experience with big data, familiar with Hive, Spark and similar tools;
4. Experience in entertainment or advertising companies will be a plus;
5. Experience with data mining and machine learning will be a plus.

Responsibilities
1. Build industry leading recommendation system; develop highly scalable classifiers and tools leveraging machine learning;
2. Understand product objectives and machine learning techniques; improve model and recommendation strategy;
3. Understand user behavior and apply ML algorithms to optimize content consumption and production experience;
4. Understand content security strategy and apply ML algorithms to improve content audit process;
5. Work with TikTok cross functional teams to grow TikTok in important markets.
Qualifications
1. Bachelor degree in computer science or a related technical discipline, with 2+ years of related work experience;
2. Strong experience with data structures or algorithms;
3. Software development experience through hands on coding in a general purpose programming language;
4. Experience in one or more of the following areas: machine learning, recommendation systems, data mining or other related areas;
5. Strong communication and teamwork skills;
6. Passion about techniques and solving challenging problems.

Location: Kansas City, MO / Remote
Responsibilities:
Responsible for the development and integration of new or existing applications into the technical infrastructure and existing business processes;
Provide technical or functional guidance to project or work teams as needed within a specific discipline;
Analyze, design, develop, test, debug, implement, maintain and/or enhance existing or new systems that are reliable and efficient;
Extend company’s data with third party sources of information when needed;
Enhance data collection procedures to include information that is relevant for building analytic systems;
Verify integrity of data used for analysis;
Do ad-hoc analysis and present results in a clear manner;
Requirements:
Experience working as an IT Data Scientist (5+ years);
Experience with common data science toolkits, such as R, MatLab, etc;
Experience with data visualisation tools, such as PowerBI and others;
Experience using query languages such as SQL, Hive, etc;
Experience with NoSQL databases, such as MongoDB, HBase, etc;

Farmers Edge is a global leader in digital agriculture delivering cutting-edge solutions powered by a unique combination of field-centric data, artificial intelligence and complete integration. Since 2005, Farmers Edge has dominated the industry with disruptive technologies and strategic partnerships designed to enhance connectivity across the entire agricultural ecosystem. With the most comprehensive platform on the market-FarmCommand™-Farmers Edge is revolutionizing the way farmers, agricultural professionals and agri-businesses interact with data. Moving at the speed of digital with an elite team focused on innovation, machine learning and IoT, Farmers Edge is creating new opportunities for all stakeholders shaping the future of agriculture worldwide.
To learn more about Farmers Edge, visit FarmersEdge.ca.
Soil Sampler - Term

Location: Ames, IA and surrounding area. Specific location may be negotiable.
Employment:
F/T Term with possibility of extension
Available for up to 40+ hours/wk
Available to work weekdays and weekends

Reporting to the Hub Operations Manager, the Seasonal Soil Sampler collects soil samples according to established methods and techniques using vehicles and quads with GPS equipment and soil sampling probes. They are responsible for ensuring quality control of samples and accurate recording of information.
Duties may include the following:
Travel to assigned rural locations to take core soil samples from grower's fields;
Record sample data accurately;
Meet with supervisor regularly to discuss field conditions;
Database administration and upkeep;
Safe operation of motorized vehicles;
Those services reasonably related the performance of the foregoing duties; and
Other duties as assigned.
Education and Experience
Valid driver's license for designated state of employment;
Some agricultural experience would be an asset;
Ability to carry up to 20 kg;
Ability to travel up to 25% of the time.

We thank all applicants for their interest, however only those candidates selected for interviews will be contacted.

Organization: Corporate Functions/Legal and Commercial Services

Location: USA (East Coast or Central locations are preferred)

Accenture is a leading global professional services company, providing a broad range of services and solutions in strategy, consulting, digital, technology and operations. Combining unmatched experience and specialized skills across more than 40 industries and all business functions — underpinned by the world’s largest delivery network — Accenture works at the intersection of business and technology to help clients improve their performance and create sustainable value for their stakeholders. With 469,000 people serving clients in more than 120 countries, Accenture drives innovation to improve the way the world works and lives. Visit us at www.accenture.com.

People in the Corporate Function career track contribute to the running of Accenture as a high- performance business through specialization within a specific functional area, and grow into internally focused roles by deepening their skills and/or developing new skills within an internal functional area.

Legal and Commercial Services professionals deliver and coordinate legal, contract and commercial advice and counsel in support of Accenture's or our clients' business, working to manage and mitigate risk and ensure ethical behavior and compliance with laws and company policies.

Job Description:

The Global Services Legal team is seeking to appoint a senior counsel with 10+ years legal experience to act as Intelligent Products And Platforms Legal Lead. In-house, public sector and private practice candidates will all be considered, but experience of working with international teams in a global business and a passion for supporting innovative technology and taking products and services to market are pre-requisites.

The Intelligent Products and Platforms Business supports our clients to build platform-based business and operating models. The Business architects, designs, develops, and builds software, hardware and scalable products to help clients transform their organizations and launch new businesses, directly linking engineering and product development to increase speed to market and unlock new sources of growth.
Our strategy helps our clients navigate the shift to products as-a-service model, incentivizing and integrating service provider ecosystems, and using AI powered solutions to enhance aftermarket services such as warranty and maintenance to help our clients improve product reliability and customer loyalty to increase predictability and profitability of service revenue.

You will report into the Industry X.0 Global Legal Lead as part of the Global Legal Services Team, whose mission is to drive sustainable business growth for Accenture by providing deep expertise at the intersection of business strategy, industry and technology services in the development and ongoing support of client offerings in a highly dynamic environment. Accenture’s Services are:
Strategy & Consulting is the home of our Strategy practitioners, industry and functional expertise, data insight and design and is where our Intelligent Products and Platforms Business sits.
Interactive are a new breed of agency designed from the ground up to empower clients to own Experience, through customer-centered service design and innovation, from start to finish.
Technology anticipates future trends and brings our solutions to clients.
Operations provides business process services to drive business and financial outcomes for clients.
Intelligent Products and Platforms
The Intelligent Products and Platforms Business is a key business within Strategy & Consulting and plays a critical role in Accenture’s Go to Market strategy. You will act as a trusted advisor to senior business leadership, collaborating with senior stakeholders across the Business, across Legal and other Corporate Functions.

You will:
Provide input into, and shape strategic decisions, which impact Accenture’s Go to Market approach for the Business, including conducting portfolio level risk reviews and developing risk mitigation strategies (contractual, operational and technical) across multiple jurisdictions;
Lead cross-functional project teams (internal and external counsel) on complex, nuanced initiatives to produce high quality outcomes;
Play a key role in escalations and Accenture’s overall governance and risk management policies & processes;
Develop and roll out training to increase the industry acumen of Legal, and Sales & Delivery teams; and
Utilize excellent networking and collaboration skills to cascade insights to the wider Legal organization.
Responsibilities
Shape Offerings & Solutions: Conduct assessments and provide recommendations and tools that mitigate risks while helping shape innovative commercial models in compliance with government frameworks, policies and processes and internal policies;
Regulatory Compliance: Work with Accenture’s regulatory and compliance counsel to synthesize and apply regulatory and compliance advice, including future-looking projections of any anticipated regulatory changes potentially impacting the Business;
Client Opportunity: Provide contracting tools such as guidance and templates to Business and Legal teams to enable their day-to-day contracting. You will support relevant approvals and escalations;
Problem Projects & Delivery Issues: Support the Accenture Quality & Risk organization, litigation team and Business in the development of remediation strategies;
Responsible Business: Work with other teams and participate in initiatives to create frameworks related to cutting edge, cross-industry topics that address technology, ethics, human rights, legal and societal issues;
Thought Leadership: Collaborate with the Business and Legal in shaping commercial and regulatory environments through support of thought leadership activities;
V&A: Support Accenture’s Ventures & Acquisitions Business and Legal leadership in evaluating prospective acquisition targets, development of PMI strategy and divestiture activity;
Strategic Alliance & Partnerships: Shape new third-party strategic alliances and partnerships, including capability sourcing via vendor and resale/agency transactions; and
Business Operations Projects: Adjust Accenture policies and procedures to accommodate the requirements of the Business.

Basic Qualifications:
JD degree or equivalent degree or legal qualification.
Admitted to the bar (or local equivalent) and in good standing or otherwise authorized to practice law. A Common Law qualification is required.
Minimum of 10 years’ legal experience of relevant attorney work (some of which will have been gained at a leading law firm) supporting cutting-edge technologies particularly in digital manufacturing, digital twin development and deployment and Internet of Things, cloud computing, software embedded in devices, artificial intelligence, edge computing etc.;
Preferred Qualifications:

Experience in advising on the development and launch of new technology products, from ideation through to go to market;
Risk analysis, appreciation and management;
Deep expertise in relation to product liability risk and mitigation in a B2B and B2C context;
Strong commercial & transactional, IP/IT and data protection experience and broad legal knowledge;
Understanding of technology and global trends impacting provision of services/products, including digital tools, use of data and new technologies;
Awareness of applicable regulatory landscapes and the effect on product development & deployment;
Extensive experience of analysis and synthesis of complex facts and situations to achieve outcomes;
Developing trusted relationships with senior business leaders, particularly for functions that have not worked extensively with legal;
Strong program management and pathfinding skills, leading diverse teams to achieve defined outcomes;
Deal shaping and innovative commercial modelling expertise;
Ability to influence and manage multiple stakeholders and other parts of Legal to drive successful results; and
Co-ordinating and overseeing the activities of external counsel and managing legal budget.

Professional Skills:
Resilient, demonstrating comfort adapting to new circumstances in a dynamic and demanding workplace;
Self-motivated, enjoy working hard and being continually challenged;
Comfortable with ambiguity;
Pragmatic and client-focused - enjoying talking to colleagues, understanding their requirements and helping problem solve to balance risk with commercial considerations;
Emotionally intelligent, able to deal with people from different countries, cultures and backgrounds and with varying skill sets. You will need to be able to understand different viewpoints, motivations and thought processes to attain a legally appropriate business solution;
A team-player, but able to work independently and unsupervised;
Interested in technology solutions;
Possessing of exceptional organisational and communication skills; and
Willing to work global hours where necessary and to travel occasionally.
Proficient at speaking English.
Demonstrated leadership in professional setting; either military or civilian.
Demonstrated teamwork and collaboration in a professional setting; either military or civilian.
Applicants for employment in the US must have work authorization that does not now or in the future require sponsorship of a visa for employment authorization in the United States and with Accenture.
Candidates who are currently employed by a client of Accenture or an affiliated Accenture business may not be eligible for consideration.
Accenture is an EEO and Affirmative Action Employer of Females/Minorities/Veterans/Individuals with Disabilities.

Equal Employment Opportunity
All employment decisions shall be made without regard to age, race, creed, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, citizenship status or any other basis as protected by federal, state, or local law.

Job candidates will not be obligated to disclose sealed or expunged records of conviction or arrest as part of the hiring process.

